<title>SWITZERLAND: CS Holding shareholders bless name change.</title>
<headline>CS Holding shareholders bless name change.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>CS Holding shareholders approved the board of director's proposal to change the company's name to Credit Suisse Group as of January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>In response to a shareholder comment, Chairman Rainer Gut said the name change would cost the group an estimated 60 million to 70 million Swiss francs.</p>
<p>The new name stems from the company's reorganisation, decided earlier this year, into four operating divisions.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
